## E. Publicity

PIC meetings are open to the public30 and meeting minutes are posted on the Knesset’s website.31 Open access does not apply, however, to minutes of hearings on issues determined by the KHC to affect “state security, its foreign relations or an essential economic interest” (essential state interests).32

As in other types of Knesset committees, full or partial public access to minutes of PIC hearings may also be limited upon a determination by the committee’s chairman for the protection of essential state interests, the interests of a minor or any other “helpless” person, or “at the request of the person who attended the meeting[that] submitting the protocol for public review may cause harm to him or others.”33 Limitation of access under these conditions, however, does not affect the right of MKs to review the meeting minutes of a committee or subcommittee on which they serve as permanent members or as permanent deputy members.34 Such limitation similarly does not apply to persons who attended the committee meeting and wish to review the minutes;

